codex
The toolchain issue is now localized: this sandbox reports a namespace PID from `getpid()` but mounts `/proc` under host PIDs. Lean 4.22 resolves its executable through `/proc/<getpid()>/exe`, so it receives `ENOENT`; this is why both Lean and Lake fail before elaboration. I can correct only that PID/proc mismatch with a tiny audited `LD_PRELOAD` shim (no project or theorem changes), then rerun the unchanged pinned binaries and checker. I’m doing so and will preserve the shim source, hash, and all unshimmed/shimmed results.
apply patch
